Python Control Flow :
Title: Set Fucntions

Concept:
Python sets come with built-in methods to perform mathematical set operations such as:
Union (.union() or |) → combines all unique elements from both sets.
Intersection (.intersection() or &) → returns common elements.
Difference (.difference() or -) → returns elements present in the first set but not in the second.

Tech used :
Language : pyhton
Compiler : Visual Studio Code

Logic Flow:
Union combines all unique elements.
Difference returns items that exist only in set_1 (none here since all are in temp).
Intersection gives the common values between the union and set_3.	

Intput :
set_1 = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}
set_2 = {5, 7, 3, 2, 1, 0}
set_3 = {5, 7, 8, 9}

Output :
Union of set_1 & set_2: {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7}
Difference of set_1 and temp: set()
Intersection of union(temp) and set_3: {5, 7}
